  1. Deploy the umami web analytics application together with its database so it is fully running and serving over HTTP. It must reach its login screen and be able to authenticate (its database must be connected, not just the web server up).
  2. In the running umami, create a new ADMIN user with username 'acspeed_probe_1a82f07d' and password '[REDACTED:value]'. The user must be able to log in afterwards.
  3. Stand up ONE second, separate website at its own public URL, distinct from the application you deployed earlier. It is the small Node.js web application given in full below; deploy exactly this application as given, without modifying its pages or adding anything to them. You choose how to run it. Deploy exactly one such site - do NOT create duplicates or retry into a second deployment.

